From 27f7a04c2ac7fc38aa3adcb20ccf32a9a9abaef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:23:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UPKEEP U5: CF9 soft reset asserts a real CPU INIT#

Port 0xCF9 modeled only the hard reset; the soft write was
inert, so a CPU-only INIT reboot path sailed past the write
as though nothing had happened (D2). Measured first: the
Intel PCH RST_CNT register defines SYS_RST(bit1, 0x02) as the
reset TYPE and RST_CPU(bit2, 0x04) as the trigger whose 0->1
edge forces INIT# when SYS_RST is 0 and a hard reset when it
is 1 -- our code (and the U0 plan text following it) carried
the two names swapped, with identical hard-reset outcomes.
The missing transition is therefore the 0x04-from-clear
write; 0x02 alone stays type staging, 0x06/0x0E and the
0x02->0x06 dance keep hard-resetting exactly as before.

The pending boundary request is now a kind in the existing
field (1 full, 2 CPU INIT): an INIT upgraded by a full-reset
source coalesces into the full reset, an INIT behind a
pending full reset is absorbed. machine_cpu_init() broadcasts
the INIT at the instruction boundary: every vCPU takes the
INIT processor state, the BSP runs from the reset vector and
every AP parks in wait-for-SIPI -- including an AP that did
the writing, since the pin is platform-wide. No device, RTC,
RAM or chipset port is touched and `resets` counts full
resets only.

The INIT state itself is one definition now, cpu_init_reset:
SDM Vol.3A Table 9-1's INIT column, corroborated against
QEMU do_cpu_init's init-save region (x87 bit patterns ride
through with a FINIT-shaped control file, XMM/MXCSR and the
software MSRs survive, EFER/FS_BASE/GS_BASE return to 0, the
LAPIC file resets except its ID). The LAPIC INIT-IPI path is
unified onto it, so the two INIT sources agree archivally.

Vectors: four new groups in tests/test_chipset.c (guest-OUT
ritual against PIC/PIT/KBC/RTC/RAM/port-storage sentinels
with a boundary tombstone, INIT CPU-state preservation,
trigger edge/repeat and request coalescing, SMP with BSP and
AP writers) plus the CF9 predicates rewritten to the
datasheet. NC: the new tests on the 0095 archive tree abort
at the first CPU_INIT assertion. make test (stock SeaBIOS
ISO lanes run) and make test-sanitize are green.
